<title>GERMANY: Russia paid $95 mln under bank debt deal last week.</title>
<headline>Russia paid $95 mln under bank debt deal last week.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG said on Monday that Russia's Vnesheconombank had on Friday transferred $95 million to a trust account held with the Bank of England under a debt rescheduling accord with its creditor banks.</p>
<p>The payment was the 10th instalment of the cash down payment under the Russian debt accord reached in principle in November 1995, Deutsche, which chairs the bank advisory committee, said.</p>
<p>The payments made by Vnesheconombank since February 1995 now amount to $1.665 billion, Deutsche said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
